{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795845486,"nonce":"OxfOlAhIoGYSa1EzSTi9iLPakJo=","title":"Show gates that are waiting, and gates rejected recently, in the UI and the API","message":"Owner request, 2026-11-28, made while deciding that agents may reject gates.\n\nAn agent acting for a person through a plugin can reject a pending gate (gate.reject is on the closed list of delegable operations; gate.approve never is). A rejection by an agent must be easy for people to notice, and a gate waiting on a person must be easy to find.\n\nWhat is wanted:\n- UI: one place that lists gates waiting for the viewer or their org, and gates rejected recently, with who rejected each one. When the DelegationTrail says a token or a plugin installation acted, show that (an agent rejected it on behalf of \u003cperson\u003e, through \u003cplugin\u003e).\n- API: the same two lists as read routes, so tools and plugins can show them. Decide which ApiOperation they fall under (run.read fits).\n- The Run page already shows a gate's state; check that a rejection shows the trail too.\n\nOpen points:\n- How far back 'recently' goes.\n- Whether the dashboard's action inbox is the place for the waiting list.\n- Whether a rejection by an agent should notify the person it acted for.\n\nRelated: ADR-0086 (delegated calls, DelegationTrail), the fork approval gate.","files":null}]}